*** Add File: DOCKER_README.md
+This folder adds a simple Docker-based local environment for the site.
+
+Quick steps
+
+1. Copy and edit environment:
+
+   cp .env.example .env
+   # Edit .env: set MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD and MYSQL_PASSWORD and replace GALLERY_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH
+
+2. Start stack:
+
+   docker compose up -d
+
+3. Generate admin password hash (on host):
+
+   php -r "echo password_hash('your-admin-password', PASSWORD_DEFAULT) . PHP_EOL;"
+   # paste the result into GALLERY_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH in .env
+
+4. Initialize DB table (run once):
+
+   docker exec -i lana_db mysql -u root -p${MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD} ${MYSQL_DATABASE} <<'SQL'
+   CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gallery_items (
+     id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
+     slug VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
+     title VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
+     medium VARCHAR(255) DEFAULT '',
+     genre VARCHAR(255) DEFAULT '',
+     description TEXT,
+     thumbnail_path VARCHAR(1024),
+     full_path VARCHAR(1024),
+     date_added DATE,
+     sold TINYINT(1) DEFAULT 0,
+     disabled TINYINT(1) DEFAULT 0,
+     is_active TINYINT(1) DEFAULT 1,
+     created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
+   ) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4;
+   SQL
+
+5. Test:
+
+   # API status
+   curl 'http://localhost:8000/gallery-api.php?action=status'
+
+   # phpMyAdmin: http://localhost:8080 (user/password from .env)
+
+Stop & cleanup
+
+   docker compose down
+   docker compose down -v   # remove volumes (DB + uploads)
+
+Notes
+- Do NOT commit `.env`.
+- `uploads` are stored in the named volume `uploads_data`; if you prefer a host folder, change the `volumes` mapping for `web`.
+
